      <workList xml:id="workDesc_2c40f20d">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e219216">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_38769801">A1:011</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_d232b3bf" xml:lang="it">I Concerto a violino principale, 2 violini, viola e basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_e5c9de27">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_45418f12">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_5c175a6e">
               <p xml:id="idm76">The present violin concerto, which seems to have been lost, is listed in two of the Breitkopf catalogues (1764 and 1766) of which the latter includes an incipit. In his autobiography (Mattheson, <rend xml:id="idm77" fontstyle="italic">Grundlage</rend>, 1740; SchW C5:001), Scheibe mentions that at that time he had already composed more than thirty concertos for the violin. The work also appears in Breitkopf’s auction catalogue of 1836 in a lot together with works by <persName xml:id="idm78" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Angelo Maria Scaccia</persName> and <persName xml:id="idm79" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Christoph Schaffrath</persName>.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_e5f0b4ce">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
            </langUsage>
